                                        Veterinary costs are one of the biggest costs for a breeder:
                                        <ul class="f-20" style="list-style-type: disc; line-height: 32px;">
                                            <li class="my-2">The cat needs several vaccinations, which often amounts to €25 to €50 per vaccination, depending on which part of the world you live in.</li>
                                            <li class="my-2">The cat also needs a chip that varies between €25 and €35 ​​per kitten.</li>
                                            <li class="my-2">The cat must also have a rabies vaccination if it goes abroad, which usually costs around €25 and €40 per kitten.</li>
                                            <li class="my-2">Many breeders also have their cats neutered or sterilized to prevent litters being created without a contract, which costs €100 to €150 per cat.</li>
                                            <li class="my-2">All cats also need a passport 15€ to 30€ per cat.</li>
                                            <li class="my-2">Deworming must also be given 3 times during the kitten period.</li>
                                            <li class="my-2">Often the parents still have to be tested for, for example: FIV/FELV HCM/PKD, but the price varies considerably from breed to breed, depending on the vet, but a test easily costs €100 to €150 per cat.</li>
                                            <li class="my-2">There are also people who still do an X-ray.</li>
                                        </ul>
